\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every complex function f on the circle with integral |f| log(2+|f|) finite, do the symmetric Fourier partial sums $S_N$ f converge to f almost everywhere as N ranges through all positive integers?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every complex function f on the circle with integral |f| log(2+|f|) finite, do the symmetric Fourier partial sums $S_N$ f converge to f almost everywhere as N ranges through all positive integers?

